# Navigate point-to-point to an absolute map-frame pose, independent of the
# coverage planner. Target must lie inside an authorized area (mowing or
# navigation-only, see MapArea.msg's is_navigation_area) — BoundaryGuard and
# LocalizationGuard protect the transit exactly as they protect mowing (their
# only exemption for this command is the blade-off dock transit, as for
# mowing). The blade is never enabled on this path.
#
# Accepted only from a settled, undocked rest state. Otherwise success=false
# and nothing changes; reason is one of:
#   invalid_pose            x, y or yaw is NaN/Inf
#   busy                    a mission (a GOTO included) or a transition is
#                           active — no hot pre-emption; send COMMAND_STOP,
#                           wait for IDLE, then a new request
#   critical_dock_failure   a critical-battery docking failed; an operator
#   critical_charge_hold    command / the charge hold must be resolved first
#   battery_charge_pending  a battery-driven dock/charge is unfinished;
#                           COMMAND_STOP or COMMAND_HOME releases it
#   docked                  on the charger or mid-undock (GOTO does not undock)
#   heading_not_calibrated  no heading seed yet this session
#   localization_degraded   the localization-degraded latch is set
#   battery_unknown         no recent valid battery voltage
#   battery_low             at or below the low-battery docking level
#   maintenance_active
#   unsupported_tree        the loaded behavior tree lacks a branch GOTO
#                           relies on (IdleSequence, StopHoldSequence,
#                           GotoSequence) — logged at startup
#
# An accepted request revokes any fleet ownership (~/fleet_yield), like every
# other accepted operator command.
#
# Returns success=true if the request was accepted; the actual navigation
# outcome is reported via /behavior_tree_node/high_level_status, briefly,
# before the tree returns to IDLE: GOTO_REACHED, GOTO_FAILED,
# GOTO_LOW_BATTERY_DOCKED, GOTO_LOW_BATTERY_DOCK_FAILED or
# GOTO_CRITICAL_BATTERY_DOCKED. No request ID correlates a status with a
# request and the status is not latched: subscribe to high_level_status BEFORE
# calling this service, then wait for GOTO_ACTIVE after success and for the
# next terminal name (or a non-GOTO state if the GOTO was interrupted).
float64 x
float64 y
float64 yaw
---
bool success
string reason
